{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788457814-kJcX9J85dhBLwzl2xALY","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything is done. Let me summarize for the user:\n\n1. Change in `dspy/predict/predict.py:_forward_preprocess` (dspy/predict/predict.py:111-123)\n2. Tests added\n3. Test results: 35 passed in test_predict.py; broader suites pass except 2 pre-existing failures.\n\nAlso mention how to use it and caveats (works for Predict and subclasses like ChainOfThought; config params like temperature must go through config={} / constructor, which is standard DSPy behavior; the prediction reaches litellm's `prediction` parameter which OpenAI supports for gpt-4o etc.).","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"daf4bd95-90eb-4bd5-a8b2-615c44312155","uuid":"68556a3f-cce1-494c-bd89-276f379537f0","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:50:21.160Z","request_id":"gen-1788457814-kJcX9J85dhBLwzl2xALY"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788457814-kJcX9J85dhBLwzl2xALY","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. DSPy now recognizes OpenAI's predicted outputs format and routes it to the LM call as a config parameter.\n\n## The change\n\nIn `Predict._forward_preprocess` (`dspy/predict/predict.py:111`), right after the temperature logic, the inputs are inspected: a `prediction` kwarg is treated as a predicted output only if it's a dict with `type == \"content\"` and a `content` key. When it matches, it's popped from `kwargs` (the regular input data) and placed into `config` (the LM call parameters), so the adapter/LM receives it as the OpenAI `prediction` parameter rather than as prompt data. Anything else named `prediction` — a string, a dict with a different `type`, a dict missing `content` — is left untouched as a normal input field, so signatures with a legit `prediction` field are unaffected.\n\nThis sits in the single preprocessing path shared by `forward` and `aforward`, so sync and async both work, and it applies to `Predict` and all its subclasses (`ChainOfThought`, etc.). Because `config` flows into the litellm request, the value also becomes part of the cache key — distinct predictions won't collide.\n\n## Verification\n\n- End-to-end check with a real `dspy.LM`: `program(question=..., prediction={\"type\": \"content\", \"content\": \"...\"})` puts `prediction` into the litellm request dict and it does not appear in the rendered user message.\n- Added 5 tests in `tests/predict/test_predict.py` covering: valid prediction moved to LM kwargs and removed from messages, coexistence with `config={\"temperature\": 0.5}`, the async path, and three malformed variants staying as regular input data.\n- `tests/predict/test_predict.py`: **35 passed**. Broader `tests/predict tests/adapters tests/clients`: 124 passed, 8 skipped, 2 failed — I confirmed via `git stash` that those 2 JSON-adapter tests fail identically on the clean tree (environment-related, not from this change).\n\nOne usage note matching existing DSPy conventions: sampling parameters like temperature must be passed as `config={\"temperature\": 0.5}` or at construction (`dspy.Predict(..., temperature=0.5)`); a bare `temperature=0.5` kwarg on the call is treated as input data in this codebase, which is why the coexistence test uses `config`.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"daf4bd95-90eb-4bd5-a8b2-615c44312155","uuid":"66012c2c-486e-4546-a1e9-a2295bee2976","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:50:33.327Z","request_id":"gen-1788457814-kJcX9J85dhBLwzl2xALY"}
