a dict with a different `type`, a dict missing `content` — is left untouched as a normal input field, so signatures with a legit `prediction` field are unaffected.\n\nThis sits in the single preprocessing path shared by `forward` and `aforward`, so sync and async both work, and it applies to `Predict` and all its subclasses (`ChainOfThought`, etc.). Because `config` flows into the litellm request, the value also becomes part of the cache key — distinct predictions won't collide.\n\n## Verification\n\n- End-to-end check with a real `dspy.LM`: `program(question=..., prediction={\"type\": \"content\", \"content\": \"...\"})` puts `prediction` into the litellm request dict and it does not appear in the rendered user message.\n- Added 5 tests in `tests/predict/test_predict.py` covering: valid prediction moved to LM kwargs and removed from messages, coexistence with `config={\"temperature\": 0.5}`, the async path, and three malformed variants staying as regular input data.\n- `tests/predict/test_predict.py`: **35 passed**. Broader `tests/predict tests/adapters tests/clients`: 124 passed, 8 skipped, 2 failed — I confirmed via `git stash` that those 2 JSON-adapter tests fail identically on the clean tree (environment-related, not from this change).\n\nOne usage note matching existing DSPy conventions: sampling parameters like temperature must be passed as `config={\"temperature\": 0.5}` or at construction (`dspy.Predict(..., temperature=0.5)`); a bare `temperature=0.5` kwarg on the call is treated as input data in this codebase, which is why the coexistence test uses `config`.","ttft_ms":10556,"type":"result","duration_ms":575893,"uuid":"b402bccb-088e-4542-8e51-e09c5aaeb948","ttft_stream_ms":3730,"time_to_request_ms":409,"queued_turn_count":0}
